# Architecture

- Route UI, layouts, loading, and error boundaries belong in `app/`.
- Reusable UI belongs in `components/`; feature logic stays beside its route until shared.
- Prefer Server Components and server-side data access.
- Isolate browser APIs and interactivity in small Client Components.
- Use Route Handlers for HTTP endpoints and validate data at boundaries.
- Keep tests next to the behavior they cover.
